# 基础词 Unit19
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-基础词
# 描述: 基础词Unit19核心词汇

{{evaluate}}{/ɪˈvæljueɪt/}}v. 评估；评价}}{{The committee will evaluate all the applications carefully.}}
{{even}}{/ˈiːvn/}}adv. 甚至；adj. 平坦的；偶数的}}{{Even the smallest contribution can make a difference.}}
{{evening}}{/ˈiːvnɪŋ/}}n. 傍晚；晚上}}{{We went for a walk in the park on a cool evening.}}
{{event}}{/ɪˈvent/}}n. 事件；活动}}{{The charity event raised over $100,000.}}
{{eventually}}{/ɪˈventʃuəli/}}adv. 最终；终于}}{{After years of hard work, she eventually achieved her goal.}}
{{evidence}}{/ˈevɪdəns/}}n. 证据；迹象}}{{There is strong evidence to support the theory.}}
{{evil}}{/ˈiːvl/}}adj. 邪恶的；n. 邪恶}}{{The hero fought against the evil forces.}}
{{evolution}}{/ˌiːvəˈluːʃn/}}n. 进化；发展}}{{The theory of evolution was proposed by Darwin.}}
{{evolve}}{/ɪˈvɒlv/}}v. 进化；发展}}{{Technology has evolved rapidly over the past decade.}}
{{exact}}{/ɪɡˈzækt/}}adj. 精确的；准确的}}{{The exact time of the meeting is 3:15 p.m.}}
{{examine}}{/ɪɡˈzæmɪn/}}v. 检查；考试}}{{The doctor examined the patient thoroughly.}}
{{example}}{/ɪɡˈzɑːmpl/}}n. 例子；榜样}}{{Can you give me an example of how this works?}}
{{exceed}}{/ɪkˈsiːd/}}v. 超过；超越}}{{Sales exceeded our expectations this quarter.}}
{{excellent}}{/ˈeksələnt/}}adj. 极好的；优秀的}}{{She received an excellent grade on her thesis.}}
{{except}}{/ɪkˈsept/}}prep. 除…之外}}{{Everyone passed the exam except Tom.}}
{{exchange}}{/ɪksˈtʃeɪndʒ/}}v./n. 交换；交流}}{{They exchanged gifts at the holiday party.}}
{{excite}}{/ɪkˈsaɪt/}}v. 使兴奋；激动}}{{The news excited the whole community.}}
{{exclude}}{/ɪkˈskluːd/}}v. 排除；排斥}}{{The price excludes tax and delivery charges.}}
{{execute}}{/ˈeksɪkjuːt/}}v. 执行；处决}}{{The plan was executed without any problems.}}
{{exercise}}{/ˈeksərsaɪz/}}n. 练习；锻炼；v. 锻炼}}{{Regular exercise is important for maintaining good health.}}
{{exhibit}}{/ɪɡˈzɪbɪt/}}v. 展示；n. 展览品}}{{The artist exhibited her work at the gallery.}}
{{exist}}{/ɪɡˈzɪst/}}v. 存在；生存}}{{Many species that once existed are now extinct.}}
{{expand}}{/ɪkˈspænd/}}v. 扩展；膨胀}}{{The company plans to expand into international markets.}}
{{expect}}{/ɪkˈspekt/}}v. 期望；预料}}{{I expect to finish the project by next week.}}
{{expense}}{/ɪkˈspens/}}n. 费用；开支}}{{Travel expenses will be covered by the company.}}
{{experience}}{/ɪkˈspɪəriəns/}}n. 经验；经历；v. 经历}}{{She has extensive experience in marketing and sales.}}
{{experiment}}{/ɪkˈsperɪmənt/}}n. 实验；v. 做实验}}{{The experiment proved the hypothesis was correct.}}
{{expert}}{/ˈekspɜːrt/}}n. 专家；adj. 熟练的}}{{The expert gave a detailed analysis of the data.}}
{{explain}}{/ɪkˈspleɪn/}}v. 解释；说明}}{{Could you explain the process in more detail?}}
{{explicit}}{/ɪkˈsplɪsɪt/}}adj. 明确的；清楚的}}{{The instructions are very explicit about the safety procedures.}}
{{explode}}{/ɪkˈspləʊd/}}v. 爆炸；爆发}}{{The firework exploded in the sky with a loud bang.}}
{{explore}}{/ɪkˈsplɔːr/}}v. 探索；考察}}{{The astronauts explored the surface of the moon.}}
{{export}}{/ɪkˈspɔːrt/}}v. 出口；n. 出口品}}{{The country exports a large amount of oil every year.}}
{{expose}}{/ɪkˈspəʊz/}}v. 暴露；揭露}}{{The report exposed the corruption in the government.}}
{{express}}{/ɪkˈspres/}}v. 表达；adj. 快速的；n. 快递}}{{She expressed her gratitude with a warm smile.}}
{{extend}}{/ɪkˈstend/}}v. 延伸；扩展}}{{The deadline has been extended by one week.}}
{{extent}}{/ɪkˈstent/}}n. 程度；范围}}{{To what extent do you agree with this statement?}}
{{external}}{/ɪkˈstɜːrnl/}}adj. 外部的；外面的}}{{The external walls of the building need painting.}}
{{extra}}{/ˈekstrə/}}adj. 额外的；n. 额外的事物}}{{You will need to pay extra for express delivery.}}
{{extraordinary}}{/ɪkˈstrɔːrdneri/}}adj. 非凡的；特别的}}{{She has extraordinary talent in music.}}
